07 Jun 2016  Robert Hatcher             (test38-V10-02-06)
----------------------------------------------------------
- CMake/CTest now playing nice with each other, so we can turn back on
  the creation & use of external additional libraries.  Only special case
  is Windows SHARED where we skip pre-linking to g4plftest38_lib1 because
  MYGEANT4_LINK_LIBRARY isn't yet refined sufficiently to build the
  necessary .lib to go with the .dll; so just explicitly load the .dll
  at run time. (needs to be able to find 'genwindef.exe')
- Coworks with phys-lists-V10-02-08 and phys-ctor-fact-V10-02-02
  and cmake-V10-02-15


06 Jun 2016  Robert Hatcher             (test38-V10-02-05)
----------------------------------------------------------
- For now don't attempt to build auxillary libraries and use the additional
  lists or physics constructors in them; what's there works, but there are
  difficulties in getting CMake and CTests to play nice and build things in
  the right places.  For now just test the factory functionality that is
  equivalent to the old factory (+ extension by direct inclusion in the
  main program source)
- Coworks with phys-lists-V10-02-08 and phys-ctor-fact-V10-02-02
  and cmake-V10-02-15


